# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Comments as a conversation with an agent (mitcad#2010, GitHub
# mitcad/Mitcad#401), on an empty design (comments-empty.json):
#   1. Add Comment with Whole Design: On hidden, nothing to pick; C1 on
#      the whole design, without a pin.
#   2. The browser's root row: Add Comment… on the whole design, C2.
#   3. An agent asks back on C1 with a long reply of several lines (as
#      MCP's reply_comment does): C1 open, waiting for your answer.
#   4. The Comments panel: the reply's row shows the reply in full in the
#      details pane, the comment's row the whole thread; selecting C1
#      selects nothing and frames nothing.
#   5. Reply… on the agent's reply shows that reply whole above the text
#      box; the user's answer ends the waiting. Reply… on the comment's row
#      answers its latest reply.
# Run by tools/ui-comments-test.sh (Linux), tools/ui-windows-comments-
# thread-test.ps1 (Windows) and tools/ui-macos-comments-thread-test.sh
# (macOS).
wait-idle
expect-ever '^Comments: none$' 30

# 1. Add Comment with Whole Design, in a design without geometry.
mark
command comment.add
wait-log '^Command Add Comment started'
wait-log '^Panel Add Comment input whole_design at '
click-logged '^Panel Add Comment input whole_design at '
wait-log '^Panel Add Comment input target at .*[(]hidden[)]$'
type-in '^Panel Add Comment input text at ' 'Plan a wall bracket for a 40 mm pipe'
mark
key Return
wait-log '^Done Add Comment$'
wait-log '^Comment added on the whole design$'
wait-log '^Comment C1: open, user, Design: Plan a wall bracket for a 40 mm pipe$'
wait-log '^Comment C1 pin: none$'
wait-log '^Comments open: 1$'

# 2. The browser's root row: Add Comment… on the whole design.
mark
context-menu-logged '^Browser Root at ' 'Add Comment…'
focus-dialog '^Add Comment$'
wait-log '^Comment dialog opened: Add Comment: Whole design$'
focus-widget commentText
type 'Name the bodies after their use'
key Return
focus-main
wait-log '^Comment added on Whole design$'
wait-log '^Comment C2: open, user, Design: Name the bodies after their use$'
wait-log '^Comments open: 2$'

# 3. The agent asks back on C1, a reply of several lines and paragraphs.
mark
model-command '{"cmd":"reply_comment","id":"C1","author":"claude-code","text":"Before I start, two questions:\n1. Which wall material is it, concrete, brick or wood?\n2. Which screws do you have at hand?\n\nUntil then I would make the bracket of 3 mm steel with two M6 holes 50 mm apart, a clamp of 40 mm inner diameter and a 15 mm wide strap, rounded at every outer corner. Tell me if any of that should change."}'
wait-log '^Comment C1 reply 1: claude-code: Before I start, two questions: / 1[.] Which wall material'

# 4. The Comments panel: the status, the reply in full, the whole thread.
mark
command view.comments
focus-dialog '^Comments$'
wait-log '^Comments status C1: Open, waiting for your answer$'
wait-log '^Comments status C2: Open$'
wait-log '^Comments row C1 reply 1 at '
mark
dialog-click-logged '^Comments row C1 reply 1 at '
wait-log '^Comments selected: C1 reply 1$'
wait-log '^Comments details: C1 reply 1: On Design, Open, waiting for your answer / Reply 1 by claude-code, .* / Before I start, two questions: / 1[.] Which wall material is it, concrete, brick or wood[?] / 2[.] Which screws do you have at hand[?] / .*a 15 mm wide strap, rounded at every outer corner[.] Tell me if any of that should change[.]$'
# Its target, the whole design: nothing selected, nothing framed.
wait-log '^Comment target shown: C1: nothing selected [(]view none[)]$'
expect-widget-property commentsDetails readOnly true
mark
dialog-click-logged '^Comments row C1 at '
wait-log '^Comments selected: C1$'
wait-log '^Comments details: C1: On Design, Open, waiting for your answer / Comment 1 by user, .* / Plan a wall bracket for a 40 mm pipe / Reply 1 by claude-code, .* / Before I start, two questions: / .*Tell me if any of that should change[.]$'

# 5. Reply… on the agent's reply: that reply whole above the text box.
mark
dialog-click-logged '^Comments row C1 reply 1 at '
wait-log '^Comments selected: C1 reply 1$'
mark
dialog-click-logged '^Comments Reply at '
focus-dialog '^Reply to Comment 1$'
wait-log '^Comment dialog answers: Reply 1 by claude-code, .*: Before I start, two questions: / .*Tell me if any of that should change[.]$'
wait-log '^Comment dialog opened: Reply to Comment 1: Design$'
expect-widget-property commentAnswering readOnly true
focus-widget commentText
type 'Concrete wall, M6 screws. The rest is fine.'
key Return
wait-log '^Comment C1 reply 2: user: Concrete wall, M6 screws[.] The rest is fine[.]$'
focus-dialog '^Comments$'
wait-log '^Comments status C1: Open$'

# Reply… on the comment's row answers its latest reply, the user's; Esc
# cancels.
mark
dialog-click-logged '^Comments row C1 at '
wait-log '^Comments selected: C1$'
wait-log '^Comments details: C1: On Design, Open / Comment 1 by user, .* / Reply 2 by user, .* / Concrete wall, M6 screws[.] The rest is fine[.]$'
mark
dialog-click-logged '^Comments Reply at '
focus-dialog '^Reply to Comment 1$'
wait-log '^Comment dialog answers: Reply 2 by user, .*: Concrete wall, M6 screws[.] The rest is fine[.]$'
focus-widget commentText
key Escape
wait-log '^Comment dialog cancelled: Reply to Comment 1$'
focus-dialog '^Comments$'
button '^Close$' commentsClose
focus-main
expect-never 'TestDriver: FAIL'
